<% content_for :title, "Hack Club NDA API Docs" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "docs-page" %>

<article class="docs-shell">
  <header class="docs-header">
    <div>
      <h1>NDA status</h1>
      <p>Check whether a Hack Club member has signed the current NDA. No authentication is required.</p>
    </div>
    <%= link_to "OpenAPI 3.1 specification", openapi_path, class: "button button-secondary docs-spec-link" %>
  </header>

  <section class="docs-endpoint" aria-labelledby="endpoint-title">
    <div class="endpoint-heading" id="endpoint-title">
      <span class="http-method">GET</span>
      <code>/api/v1/nda_status/:info</code>
    </div>
    <p>Replace <code>:info</code> with a Slack ID or URL-encoded email address.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="docs-grid">
    <section class="docs-section docs-request">
      <h2>Examples</h2>
      <h3>Slack ID</h3>
      <pre><code>GET /api/v1/nda_status/U0123ABCDEF</code></pre>
      <h3>Email</h3>
      <pre><code>GET /api/v1/nda_status/orpheus%40example.com</code></pre>
      <p>Slack IDs begin with <code>U</code> or <code>W</code>. Emails are case-insensitive; encode <code>@</code> as <code>%40</code>.</p>
      <p>Email lookup checks signing and verified account emails. Email responses omit <code>slack_id</code> and are not cached.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section docs-responses">
      <h2>Responses</h2>

      <div class="response-heading">
        <h3>Signed</h3>
        <code>200 OK</code>
      </div>
      <p>An approved current signature or legacy import returns <code>signed</code>.</p>
      <pre><code>{
  "slack_id": "U0123ABCDEF",
  "status": "signed",
  "nda_version": "<%= NdaDocument::VERSION %>",
  "signed_at": "2025-04-02T15:04:05Z",
  "signature_type": "native"
}</code></pre>

      <div class="response-heading">
        <h3>Not signed</h3>
        <code>200 OK</code>
      </div>
      <p>Unknown or unsigned members return <code>not_signed</code>, without signing details.</p>
      <pre><code>{
  "slack_id": "U0123ABCDEF",
  "status": "not_signed",
  "nda_version": "<%= NdaDocument::VERSION %>"
}</code></pre>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-grid docs-grid-secondary">
    <section class="docs-section">
      <div class="response-heading">
        <h2>Invalid input</h2>
        <code>400 Bad Request</code>
      </div>
      <p>Malformed Slack IDs return <code>invalid_slack_id</code>; malformed emails containing <code>@</code> return <code>invalid_email</code>.</p>
      <pre><code>{
  "error": "invalid_slack_id"
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <div class="response-heading">
        <h2>Rate limit</h2>
        <code>429 Too Many Requests</code>
      </div>
      <p>Each client IP may make up to 10 requests per second across the site. Additional requests receive <code>429 Too Many Requests</code> with a <code>Retry-After</code> header.</p>
      <p>Every API response, including errors, reports the budget after the request:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>RateLimit-Limit</code>: requests allowed per window.</li>
        <li><code>RateLimit-Remaining</code>: requests left the current window.</li>
        <li><code>RateLimit-Reset</code>: seconds until the window resets</li>
        <li><code>RateLimit-Policy</code> and <code>RateLimit</code>: the same quota and budget in the <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-httpapi-ratelimit-headers">IETF draft format</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>The budget is shared across the site by client IP, including failed requests. When remaining reaches zero, wait for reset. On a 429, wait at least <code>Retry-After</code> seconds before retrying. Concurrent requests may consume the remaining budget.</p>
      <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 200 OK
RateLimit-Limit: 10
RateLimit-Remaining: 9
RateLimit-Reset: 1
RateLimit-Policy: "requests-per-ip";q=10;w=1
RateLimit: "requests-per-ip";r=9;t=1</code></pre>
      <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: text/plain
RateLimit-Limit: 10
RateLimit-Remaining: 0
RateLimit-Reset: 1
RateLimit-Policy: "requests-per-ip";q=10;w=1
RateLimit: "requests-per-ip";r=0;t=1
Retry-After: 1

Retry later</code></pre>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
